dialogue cohesion_barbarian_sage
title: A knot for the living
trigger: Cohesion barbarian sage level=2
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker barbarian barbarian
speaker sage sage

node open commander
  The Sage is smearing salve into the Barbarian's split knuckles by lantern light. The knotted cord hangs from the Sage's wrist, and the Barbarian keeps glancing at it.
  -> cord

node cord barbarian
  That string of yours. The Cleric says every knot's a dead pilgrim. Is there one in there for me yet?
  -> wick

node wick sage
  Not dead. Lost. There's a difference on the Lantern Road. And no, not for you. The first one is Wick's. My apprentice. Wick's colour went thin, and Wick climbed the stair alone to fix it.
  -> carried

node carried barbarian
  Alone? Nobody stopped them? I'd have carried Wick down that stair over one shoulder, kicking.
  -> promise

node promise sage
  You'd have tried. So would I, if I'd been sure in time. Is that a promise anyone gets to make, Commander? Carrying people down?
  * I made it already. The Barbarian just said it louder. -> shared
    if: FlagSet sage:wick_promised
    do: AddCohesion barbarian sage 10
    do: SetFlag barbarian_sage:stair_shared
  * Nobody climbs alone. Let the Barbarian carry it with you. -> climbs
    do: AddCohesion barbarian sage 10
    do: AddTrust sage -2
    do: SetFlag barbarian_sage:stair_climbs
  * Promises don't bring anyone down the stair. Plans do. -> plans
    do: AddCohesion barbarian sage -4
    do: AddTrust barbarian -3
    do: SetFlag barbarian_sage:stair_plans
  * Wick is the Sage's to carry, not the Barbarian's. -> own
    do: AddCohesion barbarian sage -2
    do: AddTrust sage 2
    do: SetFlag barbarian_sage:stair_own

node shared sage
  Louder, yes. The Commander says it quietly and I half believe it. You say it like a door being kicked in and I believe all of it.
  -> cloth

node climbs sage
  Carry it with me. I've had this cord to myself for a long time. I'm not sure I know how to hand any of it over. Hold this end, then. Just hold it.
  -> cloth

node plans barbarian
  Plans. Fine. Make a plan, Commander, and put me at the top of the stair in it. That's my promise, then, written as a plan.
  -> cloth

node own barbarian
  The Sage's to carry. Fine. But if I see anyone going up that stair alone again, I'm not asking whose they are.
  -> cloth

node cloth barbarian
  Here. The white off the tithe wagon. Tie a knot in it. For me. If I don't come down, you'll have something to carry back.
  * Tie it loose, the way you tied ours. A loose knot comes undone on the way down. -> loose
    if: FlagSet sage:cord_tied
    do: AddCohesion barbarian sage 8
    do: SetFlag barbarian_sage:cloth_loose
  * No knot. The end stays clean. We're all coming down. -> clean
    if: FlagSet sage:cord_down
    do: AddCohesion barbarian sage 10
    do: SetFlag barbarian_sage:cloth_clean
  * One knot in the cloth, one in the cord. Each of you carries the other. -> traded
    do: AddCohesion barbarian sage 10
    do: AddTrust sage -3
    do: SetFlag barbarian_sage:cloth_traded
  * Nobody ties knots for the living tonight. Put it away. -> none
    do: AddCohesion barbarian sage -4
    do: SetFlag barbarian_sage:cloth_none

node loose sage
  Loose. There. A thumb could pull it. Make sure it's yours that does, Barbarian, at the bottom of the stair.
  -> close

node clean sage
  The end stays clean. I said I'd hold the Commander to that. I'll hold you to it too. Wrap your hand back up.
  -> close

node traded sage
  A knot for the living. The road would call that bad luck. The road has had a lot of bad luck lately anyway. Hold still.
  -> close

node none barbarian
  Away it goes, then. Back on the hand that swings. That's where it does most good.
  -> close

node close commander
  The Sage ties off the salve wrap. The Barbarian flexes the hand, looks at the cord on the Sage's wrist a moment longer, and goes back to the fire without a word, which from the Barbarian is a great deal.
